{"title":"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Bashy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Bashy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Summary_of_Solution_2)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Summary of Solution 2)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(enumeration_and_casework)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (enumeration and casework)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three fair six-sided dice are rolled. What is the probability that the values shown on two of the dice sum to the value shown on the remaining die?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/7/507886b0828e0f3dceb1c4fb82c359900a2674c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\dfrac16\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\dfrac{13}{72}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\dfrac7{36}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\dfrac5{24}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\dfrac29$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"395\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we note that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/f/07f55e0a11e29af7baee666c19c147e6f7c1923e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, 3, 4,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to get sums of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddcbabf98bdc898829e8753059c7d6fbe15a575.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 3, 4, 5, 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" /> respectively--this is not too hard to see. With any specific sum, there is exactly one way to attain it on the other die. This means that the probability that two specific dice have the same sum as the other is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/3/0232e2cd81c4f2dc3f7c46c1875a3ee3578cbe7e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac16 \\left( \\dfrac{1+2+3+4+5}{36}\\right) = \\dfrac{5}{72}.\\]\" width=\"228\" height=\"43\" /> Since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/6/d36ed57d9b17cf35aa42a98275a59a994033dacc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"33\" height=\"53\" /> ways to choose which die will be the one with the sum of the other two, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/e/62eae8688aa930dddd4972841b080a3043820fba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\cdot \\dfrac{5}{72} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} \\: \\dfrac{5}{24}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"136\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Bashy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Bashy)\">Solution 2 (Bashy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Bashy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/8/898c42884389f8833d82b6922690d889232afe4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 2, 3); (1, 3, 4); (1, 4, 5); (1, 5, 6); (2, 3, 5); (2, 4, 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"388\" height=\"20\" /> have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to rearrange them for a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> ways. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/f/8ff707275ea1e9f7204b00a7c1773255d3d2652d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 1, 2); (2, 2, 4); (3, 3, 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"191\" height=\"20\" /> have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to rearrange them for a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways. Adding them up, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> ways. We have to divide this values by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/b/deb727737c86860eb4f99b6878465cadb06cfc6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^3$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> because there are 3 dice. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/b/e5bffc8c4e5c1bba121784f61c2e6ec3dd9c111d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{45}{216}=\\boxed{\\dfrac{5}{24}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"91\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~MathFun1000\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Summary_of_Solution_2.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Summary_of_Solution_2)\">Solution 3 (Summary of Solution 2)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Summary of Solution 2)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Start by listing all possible sums. Then find the ways to arrange them and sum them up and divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/b/deb727737c86860eb4f99b6878465cadb06cfc6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^3$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> for 3 dice. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/5/715428c638c32ddee5dbca7a5675a053d20c2887.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{45}{216}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"29\" height=\"38\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/3/173384345edbb71eb9af2d41ca6b4801d831c499.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} \\: \\dfrac{5}{24}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"69\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>-aopspandy\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28enumeration_and_casework.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(enumeration_and_casework)\">Solution 4 (enumeration and casework)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (enumeration and casework)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to pick the dice which is the sum. From here proceed with \"casework\":\n</p>\n<ul><li>If the sum is 1, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways because the minimum sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.</li>\n<li>If the sum is 2, there is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> way (namely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/f/31fa6b94e5a84b15c9a080cd52edc749580d90c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />).</li>\n<li>If the sum is 3, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways (namely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69273482bff8727194f6407e55ac1bfa94d9c555.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/a/f7a25c234892fb8a7738bc31e5ccee3bf9ad5afc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />).</li>\n<li>If the sum is 4, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways (namely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/a/1ba3e3f9bd99ddc2bf9e6d9244ebf4bfbc3776d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/6/d261236ea904095d8d185a456444545b5206013b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/0/5506b58320deb5004bf2ed2f1a5e3e672d6e326e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />).</li></ul>\n<p>We start noticing that for a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> cases, but let's keep going to verify.\n</p>\n<ul><li>If the sum is 5, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways (namely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/1/5a1acbf245a710398f64953985490d7b1134630b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/5/78561eb59286ee78766fdc37ef35399bf0355e7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/a/68a601c8e837eafe7d899c2ba96295b3637daf6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/4/ea44bd62795a5d84c16a028ff4fb079a5cb8e63f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />).</li>\n<li>If the sum is 6, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways (namely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/b/dbb8858b7eefd40608ac2c33f75f1c80b800bc74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/5/2e5c05123d72c760159fe732b683014c75008c17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/6/4c6f0e4cd615eb4d118bf243be6594935ad3de9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1924ac42c8e1d1cb79000224acbe2c46d4b22bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/4/c04fa1d70044a676ae0a28e1476d5192f5cd8496.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />).</li></ul>\n<p>We have exhausted all cases because there is no way a dice can roll a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Summing, there are 15 ways here.\nTo summarize: there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to pick the dice that is the sum, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> ways to achieve the sum, for a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> configurations. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/1/0f15304e156091cd72fe4e8d75c3a087562df472.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6\\cdot6\\cdot6=216$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"14\" /> total configurations, and the probability is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/5/1352b6287137534c5ada8a0d0a988cc5271f8366.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{45}{216}=\\frac{5}{24} \\Longrightarrow \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} \\frac{5}{24}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"182\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~JH. L\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/5UojVH4Cqqs?t=702\">https://youtu.be/5UojVH4Cqqs?t=702</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A\">2014 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index